      "writtenOn": "2018-07-12T10:24:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the parent\u0027s limit is unset, and _get_specified_limit_value returns the registered limit, does that mean the child\u0027s limit can never exceed the registered limit unless the parent\u0027s limit is raised?\n\nI guess that makes sense, and if you didn\u0027t want that you would use the flat model, just trying to make sure I follow.\n\nIs it possible to say the registered limit is infinite, and allow child project limits to be unrestricted by their parents? We\u0027d usually indicate that with a -1 but that wouldn\u0027t work with this arithmetic logic.",
      "range": {
